The back office system maintains 4 lock files (LOCK.DAT) in various directories
these are (I assume) to make sure that the BO is not already runnung.  These
lock files do not appear to be set to the correct state when leaving the program
and must be deleted manually.  I have set up a batch file that deletes these
files, and it must be run before EACH running of BO.

If LVLO is run before BO there sometimes appears to be a confilct with one of 
the files that BO is using.  Howevr if LVLO is run afterward there is no problem.

I set up my system so that DOS had only 2.3M of free memory, and windows had
a 10M swap file.  This appears to be fine with BO,CT & LVLO rnning symulatniously.

The counter terminal program is not able to run under windows on a hercules
screen because it automatically switches the screen in to CGA 40 column mode
Therefore each of the counter terminals wil need to be fitted with a VGA
controller and a Monochrome VGA screen. This screen will need to be powered 
seperatly from the processor and will therefore take another mains power socket

The CT keyboard may need to have a special device driver so that it works 
properly with both the CT and LVLO applications.

When the CT application is shipped for these mchines iT will  need to supplly
the old printer (TM270) handling routines. And there may be issues with thw MAG 
card opperation. I cannot quantify this until I have the new MAG card and keyboard
(and the software tht uses it).


